##
##    PrePoMax --> code_aster from "pmx2aster.py" V0.1.4 | [ 01-Oct-2025 ] 
##    Made by Sound Spinning | soundspinning@hotmail.com
##    Meant to be run from a terminal with `run_aster *.export` instead of with `as_run`
##

 #  "R3_M14_bolt.inp" model HEADING:
 # Hash: AL8G1aNc, Date: 11/03/2025, Unit system: MM_TON_S_C
 # R3_M14_bolt.pmx
 # M14 Bolt preload tests: 4 Static steps
 # 1.- Cold Assy with bolt preload.
 # 2.- Relax bolt load via Y ext load.
 # 3.- Bring ext load to zero (back to preload only).
 # 4.- Increase bolt load via Y ext load.
 # 5.- Bring ext load to zero (back to preload only).
 # 6.- Relax bolt load via closing the yoke.
 # 7.- Increase bolt load via opening the yoke.
 # -----------------------------------

### RAM in MB - Since V16.7 the solver grabs 90% of this input
P memory_limit 64000
P ncpus 1
### max solve time in seconds ==> 4e5s = 4.63days 
P time_limit 400000.0

## Input deck
F comm R3_M14_bolt.comm D  1

## Input mesh - ASTER format
F mesh R3_M14_bolt.msh D  21

## Output message file
F mesg R3_M14_bolt.msg R  6

## Output text results file
F data R3_M14_bolt.dat R  8

## MED results file#1
F rmed R3_M14_bolt.rmed R  80
## MED results file#2
F rmed R3_M14_bolt_points_springs.rmed R  81

## Output FOLDER for global restart files, also useful for Sub-modelling
## When reading the `base` in a restart run, change RC --> DC
## R base R3_M14_bolt RC 0

## Output local temp FOLDER (if needed) for solver temp (.med) files
## R repe TMP R  0
